+// A `<4 x half>` read at offset 0 of a struct whose leading member is `<4 x float>` (the Apple
+// uniform union whose second arm is not in the type) reads the LOW eight bytes: lanes 0..2 of the
+// float vector, bitcast. Previously refused as "non-bitcastable pointee Struct".
